<p>(A) Non-recurring, non-cash expenses related to the extension and vesting of stock options effective with the company's public offering in June.  Excluding this charge, operating income, pro-forma net income and earnings per share would have been $2,353,000, $1,327,000 and 12 cents for the year ended Dec. 31, 1996. (B) A pro-forma provision for taxes for periods prior to the effective date of the company's offering has been computed as if the company had been fully subject to federal and state income taxes based upon the tax laws in effect during the periods.</p>
<p>Prior to the effective date, the company was subject to taxation under Subchapter S of the Internal Revenue Code. For the three months ended Dec. 31, 1996 the company had been fully subject to federal and state income taxes.</p>
